{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1v64KYcDjMm8grtXSzR", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I signed off with one bug filed and a low confidence (0.5). Several areas were not fully covered.\n\n**Bug filed (1):** In the file browser, with \"Folder first\" unticked, folder Zeta stays at the top of the list above all the files. This happens under Name sort and under Date sort. With \"Folder first\" ticked, grouping works correctly. Both sorts share the same root cause, so I filed it once.\n\n**Checked and working:**\n- **Sort:** Size, Date and Name, with reverse order, and with Folder first on and off.\n- **Line duplicate (Ctrl+D):** Correct on the first line, the last line, and a single line with no trailing newline. Undo restored each file.\n- **Search/replace:** Match counts, Replace all, Replace (1), Undo after each change, and empty search and replace fields. The replace field sits below the search field.\n- **View mode:** Plain text, nested list rendering, and rotation (view mode kept).\n\n**Not covered or only partly covered:**\n- Move line up/down.\n- MIME type and Folder local sort options.\n- Preserve Case, the Match Case, Whole Word and regex toggles.\n- The middle-line duplicate case. Keyboard interference got in the way of a clean retest.\n- Sort persistence across an app restart.\n\n**Side effects:** I did not save any file. Every test edit was undone, and Save was disabled on each file I left. Once, pressing Back closed Markor to the launcher; I reopened it and the state was intact."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 791, "cache_read_input_tokens": 278111, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 791}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformation